</div>

    <p class="mt-1 mb-6 max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                    A multiplication table lays out the product of two numbers at the intersection of their row and
            column, and is one of the most common tools for learning and referencing times tables. Hover any
            cell in the grid below to highlight its row and column headers, or jump straight to an individual
            number's table further down — every table can be printed or downloaded as a branded PDF, including
            a blank worksheet version for practice.
            </p>

            <nav class="mb-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm" aria-label="Multiplication table ranges">
            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-20 (default)</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-12" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-12</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-15" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-15</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-20" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-20</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-30" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-30</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-50" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-50</a>
                            <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/1-100" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">1-100</a>
                        <a href="https://math.tools/table/multiplication/finger-chart" class="mtools-btn rounded-full px-3 py-1 ">Finger Chart</a>
        </nav>
    
    <div class="mtools-ad my-4" style="min-height: 100px">
